& [ContextForm] carries exact admitted authority
  + [RCT-001] CoordinationToolContext is a strict versioned JSON and JsonSchema-capable form
  + [RCT-002] it contains ProcedureCatalogueState CompiledProcedureIdentity CantorProcessIr AdmissionDisposition InvocationRequest and NegotiationSession
  + [RCT-003] it contains no replay candidate history provider prompt model hidden state runtime handle or adapter-owned session identifier
  + [RCT-004] a convenience conversion from successful AuthorshipLaneEvidence copies only those six exact fields

& [CommandForm] is closed
  + [RCT-005] CoordinationToolRequest is a strict tagged BEGIN or ADVANCE union
  + [RCT-006] BEGIN contains one context and ADVANCE contains one context one CoordinationCheckpoint and maximum_steps
  + [RCT-007] CoordinationToolOperation CoordinationToolStatus CoordinationToolResult and CoordinationToolFault are typed closed forms
  + [RCT-008] CoordinationToolResponse always carries profile operation status optional result optional fault and explicit nonclaims
  + [RCT-009] succeeded carries one matching result and no fault while refused or invalid carries one fault and no result

& [PureDispatch] preserves core semantics
  + [RCT-010] BEGIN delegates to begin_coordination_checkpoint without rebuilding validation
  + [RCT-011] ADVANCE delegates to advance_coordination_checkpoint without rebuilding validation
  + [RCT-012] EvaluationFault becomes a stable string category and exact message without fabricating a checkpoint or transition
  + [RCT-013] maximum_steps equal to zero is invalid before core execution and returns no result
  + [RCT-014] equal immutable request values produce byte-equal response values without external effects or retained state

& [LocalMCP] is one bounded stateless transport
  + [RCT-015] cantor-coordination-mcp is a local STDIO executable with one tool named step_procedure_coordination
  + [RCT-016] tool input is CoordinationToolRequest and full CoordinationToolResponse is returned as structuredContent
  + [RCT-017] text content is a short nonauthoritative status summary and cannot replace structuredContent
  + [RCT-018] tool annotations declare read-only idempotent non-destructive closed-world behavior
  + [RCT-019] server ingress is bounded at 33554432 bytes and parse size internal and dispatch failures return stable MCP-visible errors
  + [RCT-020] server retains no coordination context checkpoint or result between calls

& [HostFlow] is explicitly staged
  + [RCT-021] this P0 operates only between inference passes after a host receives a complete model tool request or deterministically selects one
  + [RCT-022] a host may append returned structured content to a subsequent model pass but this project does not modify model tokens KV cache hidden state or a live forward pass
  + [RCT-023] Codex llama.cpp Ollama and other tool hosts are prospective callers and no automatic registration or provider compatibility claim is made

& [Boundary] is a callable proof-of-concept
  + [RCT-024] no process-local custody persistence ledger authentication authorization external effect model invocation prompt template IDE UI deployment or network listener is included
  + [RCT-025] digest binding remains integrity and lineage evidence rather than producer identity or semantic truth
  + [RCT-026] the existing procedure-tool CLI and schemas remain behaviorally compatible

& [Acceptance] is finite
  + [RCT-A01] source SJS signature and seven-fold trace verify
  + [RCT-A02] direct BEGIN and ADVANCE responses equal their core entrypoint values and deterministic replay is byte-equal
  + [RCT-A03] strict JSON schema unknown-field zero-quota and core refusal cases fail closed with no successor result
  + [RCT-A04] official RMCP subprocess discovery invocation structured response metadata and shutdown pass
  + [RCT-A05] formatting warnings-denied lint full workspace regression manifest audit narrative and scoped Git review pass

